+# Provisional database model
+
+Status: conceptual proposal for this trial; no adopted schema or implementation.
+Date: 2026-10-02. Revision: 1.
+
+This model can answer both [supplied retrieval questions](../../brief.md) under the assumptions below. PostgreSQL is selected by [project instructions](../../AGENTS.md); representation and implementation remain deferred. [Term meanings](../project/glossary.md) and [synthetic scenarios](scenarios.md) have separate owners.
+
+## Known facts and provisional assumptions
+
+The supplied entities are organisation, agreement and service. Participant roles and all relationship cardinalities remain undecided. For a small worked proposal:
+
+- A1: An agreement involves one or more organisations. An organisation can participate in zero or more agreements. This is a hypothesis to exercise retrieval, not a conclusion from missing requirements.
+- A2: Each agreement covers exactly one service. A service can be covered by zero or more agreements. The brief's singular wording motivates this hypothesis but does not settle cardinality.
+- A3: Involvement means a direct agreement–organisation relationship. It carries no inferred provider, customer, payer or permission role. The retrieval returns each agreement once even if later modeling introduces several roles for a participant.
+- A4: Each entity has an identity independent of its name. Synthetic identifiers below distinguish entities; storage types and identifier generation are undecided.
+
+## Canonical ER view
+
+Conceptual and provisional: **every cardinality below is assumed under A1–A2**. There are no implemented keys or tables in this view. Crow's-foot ends describe the entity next to them: `||` exactly one, `o{` zero or more, `}|` one or more. Dashed edges use Mermaid’s non-identifying notation; here they are illustrative only, with identity dependence deferred.
+
+```mermaid
+erDiagram
+    ORGANISATION }|..o{ AGREEMENT : "participates in (A1)"
+    SERVICE ||..o{ AGREEMENT : "is covered by (A2)"
+```
+
+For one agreement, follow participation to its organisations and coverage to its single service. For one organisation, reverse participation to retrieve its agreements, then follow coverage for each agreement. No direct organisation–service relationship is proposed: participation alone does not establish who supplies a service.
+
+Agreement participation and coverage are agreement-scoped facts. Organisation and service identity and naming belong to those respective concepts. Renaming does not change identity. Withdrawal, deletion, corrections and historical retention have no decided lifecycle rules; this read-only exercise does not invent them.
+
+## Choices blocking implementation
+
+1. Decide whether an agreement may have no participants, exactly one, or several; decide whether an organisation may have no agreements. This can invalidate A1 and affects required links.
+2. Define participation and its roles: which roles exist, whether they are required, and whether the same organisation can have several roles in one agreement. This determines whether a separate participation concept is needed.
+3. Decide whether an agreement may cover zero or several services and whether a service may be shared by agreements. This can invalidate A2 and changes the coverage relationship.
+4. Decide stable identifier policy, duplicate recognition and relationship uniqueness before choosing PostgreSQL representation. Names cannot serve as identity merely because the examples use distinct labels.
+5. Decide correction, withdrawal, deletion and retention behavior before any maintained implementation needs those operations.
+
+The next bounded task is to resolve participation and coverage meaning against the counterexamples, then revise this model and its scenarios together. No external owner is contacted during this trial.
+
+## Verification record
+
+2026-10-02: Reviewed both ER ends against A1–A2 and traced the two retrieval paths through the synthetic cases. Checked local documentation links and whitespace. Only one canonical ER source is maintained.
+
+No project preview/build configuration or local `mmdc` command was found. Mermaid parsing, rendered readability and theme checks were not performed. No runtime, SQL, migration, provisioning, permission or seed-loading behavior was tested. The proposal is not implementation-ready.
+
+Verification friction: the local `python` alias was absent; the documentation link check succeeded with `python3`. A word-count audit unnecessarily opened all installed guidance files to count words, although only relevant guidance text was reviewed. Future audits should use an explicit read manifest. Renderer absence leaves visual verification outstanding.
