+# Domain glossary
+
+Status: provisional meanings for the bounded trial.
+Date: 2026-10-02. Revision: 1.
+
+The [model](../database/model.md) owns relationships, assumptions and blocking choices.
+
+- **Organisation:** An identifiable organisational participant that may be linked to an agreement. A shared or changed name does not establish shared or changed identity. Its legal form is unspecified.
+- **Agreement:** An identifiable arrangement involving organisations and covering a service under the provisional model. No legal status, validity period or document format is implied.
+- **Service:** The identifiable subject covered by an agreement. Its granularity and classification are undecided.
+- **Participation / involvement:** A direct relationship between an organisation and an agreement. Its role meaning remains open; it is not an operational permission or a claim that the organisation supplies the service.
+- **Coverage:** The relationship saying which service an agreement concerns. Multiplicity belongs to the model's provisional assumptions.
+- **Identifier:** A reference that distinguishes an entity independently of its label. Example identifiers are synthetic notation, not a storage or generation decision.
+
+Participation and coverage are relationship terms, not additional adopted entities or database tables.
